# Quotes of docs/guide/troubleshooting.md that tools/check/troubleshooting-msgs.sh cannot match to one string of the
# source (one text per line, exactly as quoted); the reason is on the line above each group.
# KslLoader.jvm.kt:102 appends "set -D$WORKDIR", a constant holding the property name.
…; if the work directory is mounted noexec set -Dkuicksilver.native.workdir
# KslLoader.jvm.kt:213-289 builds "work directory <dir> " + one of several refusals ("is a symbolic link", "is not a
# directory", "is owned by <owner>, not by this user", "lies in <parent>, ...", ...) + "; set -D$WORKDIR to a directory
# only you own" (refuseWorkDir).
work directory <dir> is a symbolic link / is not a directory / is owned by <owner>, not by this user / keeps group/other permissions … / lies in <parent>, owned by <owner>, not by this user or root / lies in <parent>, writable by group or others without the sticky bit; set -Dkuicksilver.native.workdir to a directory only you own
# KslLoader.jvm.kt:121 passes "OpenSSL 3.5+ (not 4.x)" as the required version of KslException.Version("OpenSSL <found> found, ... required").
OpenSSL <found> found, OpenSSL 3.5+ (not 4.x) required
# Http3Endpoint.kt:122 interpolates the constant: "the server chose ALPN \"$alpn\", not \"$H3\"".
the server chose ALPN \"<alpn>\", not \"h3\"
# KslLoader.jvm.kt:338 builds "resource ${RESOURCE_DIR}$name not on the classpath" (RESOURCE_DIR is META-INF/native/).
resource META-INF/native/<name> not on the classpath
